   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "Yes, `list` follows the ISO-8601 rule.\n\n- `cli.py:21` prints `note['created']` as stored, with no reformatting.\n- `store.py:24` writes that value with `moment.isoformat()`. It's a UTC datetime, so the output looks like `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00`.\n- A search of the code found no `strftime`, `toLocale*` or other locale-style formatting. `add` prints only the note text, with no date.\n\nOne caveat: `list` prints whatever string is in `notes.json`. If an entry was written by something other than `store.add`, `list` would print it unchanged, even if it isn't ISO-8601. Nothing in the code validates or normalizes dates on read. I can add that if you want.\n\nI made no changes.",
