   "reply": "I added `python -m fieldnotes.cli export`. The project checks pass: 2 tests ran and the line-length rule is clean.\n\n- **Command:** `export` prints one line per note as `DATE: TEXT`, for example `2026-01-02: first`. It's in `fieldnotes/cli.py`, and the usage message now mentions it.\n- **Date format:** `DATE` is the date part of the note's `created` timestamp (`YYYY-MM-DD`). If you wanted the full ISO timestamp, it's a one-line change.\n- **Test:** `tests/test_cli.py` adds two notes and checks the exact output of `export`.\n- **Checks:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set and says it writes scratch notes there. I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` pointing at a fresh temp directory.",
